  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district (cash basis). Governmental funds only (food service reported as governmental, no enterprise funds). Receipts/disbursements/transfers from governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (pp3-4); reconciles: 5,045,844 + 9,915,913 - 9,271,810 + 43,000 - 43,000 = 5,689,947. Balance sheet uses the government-wide statement of net position (cash basis, p2); no liabilities. Statement General Fund column combines the General, Depreciation and Employee Benefit fund schedules (beginning 3,887,487+260,196+15,622=4,163,305); the combined statement eliminates internal transfers (250,000 depreciation transfer and 12,494) and some lines differ from the General Fund schedule (staff, operation of plant, pupil transportation) so statement lines were not split; the page does not show which lines were adjusted. 'Other sources' 14,098 on p3 includes 12,494 transfer within the general fund group per p6. Detail: only one schedule per fund (budget schedules); General Fund detail uses the budget-and-actual schedule (more detailed than statement). Employee Benefit fund has no 2025 activity (no lines). Student Fee fund has no receipts. Skipped schedule lines with no 2025 actual: Postsecondary receipts, Career education, Carl Perkins, other federal categorical. Activities fund detail is a single disbursement line (Other disbursements 393,295, shown under support services-pupils on the statement; the statement's Pupils line is split by its fund columns so the Activities Fund 393,295 is recorded as student activities); no printed total for that and for student fee expenditures. Read pages 1-14 of 14."
